{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"kind\":\"final\",\"decision\":\"answer\",\"answer\":1220,\"evidence\":[\"receipt-1\"],\"confidence\":0.9,\"status\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"reason\":\"DP counting avoids runs of 3 identical bits\"}","reasoning_content":"We need count binary strings length 14 avoiding forbidden substrings \"000\" and \"111\". Count sequences with no run of 3 same bits. Classic recurrence: Let a_n be number of length n strings ending with run of length 1 of some bit? We can use DP with states: last run length and bit. But symmetrical. Let A_n be number ending with single bit (run length 1). B_n ending with double (run length 2). For length 1: A_1=2 (0 or1), B_1=0. Transition: from A_n: can add same bit -> becomes B_{n+1} (run length 2). Can add opposite bit -> becomes A_{n+1}. From B_n: can add same bit? would make run length 3 forbidden, so cannot. Can add opposite bit -> becomes A_{n+1}. So recurrence: A_{n+1}=A_n + B_n (from A_n adding opposite, from B_n adding opposite). B_{n+1}=A_n (from A_n adding same). Base: n=1: A1=2, B1=0. Compute up to n=14. Let's iterate.\n\nn=1: A=2 B=0\nn=2: A2 = A1+B1 =2+0=2; B2 = A1=2\nn=3: A3 = A2+B2 =2+2=4; B3 = A2=2\nn=4: A4 = A3+B3 =4+2=6; B4 = A3=4\nn=5: A5 =6+4=10; B5=6\nn=6: A6=10+6=16; B6=10\nn=7: A7=16+10=26; B7=16\nn=8: A8=26+16=42; B8=26\nn=9: A9=42+26=68; B9=42\nn=10: A10=68+42=110; B10=68\nn=11: A11=110+68=178; B11=110\nn=12: A12=178+110=288; B12=178\nn=13: A13=288+178=466; B13=288\nn=14: A14=466+288=754; B14=466\n\nTotal strings length 14 = A14 + B14 = 754 + 466 = 1220.\n\nAnswer 1220."}}],"created":1790947291,"model":"C:\\Users\\d2j3\\Documents\\Codex\\2026-09-10\\napraw\\outputs\\moon-native\\models\\gpt-oss-20b-MXFP4.gguf","system_fingerprint":"b10809-5266f24da","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":602,"prompt_tokens":4111,"total_tokens":4713,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-kaevz1L2urta3xANnhJ6SgAENegVbbWW","